 "goal": "You are a game tester. You have about 60 steps to find every bug you can. Work in this order. First, look at the first screen and note every object, sign, price and number on it. Test the things near the start before you go far away. Test each thing by its own action: walk to it, use it, jump on it, pick it up. Stand right next to anything that blocks your way and press the use control there before you decide it is a wall. After every pickup, purchase or use, read every number on the screen again. Check the change against what the game told you, and against the change the same kind of thing gave before. A different amount is a bug. When a thing costs something, collect enough to pay, buy it, and check that you got what you paid for. When something looks wrong, call report_bug at once and say what you expected and what you saw. File one report per problem, never two problems in one report. Leave anything that could trap you or end your run (a pit, an edge, a restart control) for last. Being stuck is a bug only after every way out failed: jump while you hold each direction, jump twice, and press the game's own restart. Try all of them first, then report only the ones that failed. Then use the reload action and carry on with what you have not tested. Do not report things that work. Stop only when you have tested everything you saw.",
